HTTP handlers returning response.Response can now expose Metadata as a top-level JSON response member while retaining custom-header handling. A Response with nil metadata is currently serialized as "metadata": null, which conflicts with the updated documentation's claim that the field is omitted.

Likely behavioral changes
  • When a handler result is a response.Response, the framework keeps the wrapper after applying its custom headers and passes its Data and Metadata into the HTTP response envelope. Callers can therefore observe metadata alongside the data payload.
  • A response.Response with no metadata is serialized with an explicit top-level "metadata": null member rather than a data-only envelope, as codified by the updated responder test.

